---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="Disclaimer for Simply Plant Care — the limits of our guides and tools."
  canonicalPath="/disclaimer/"
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page">Disclaimer</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
  <p class="article-meta">Last updated: 24 November 2026</p>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      The content on Simply Plant Care is general information about indoor
      plant care. It is not professional advice, and it is not a substitute
      for advice from a qualified horticulturist, nursery, or plant
      specialist.
    </p>
    <h2>Plant health</h2>
    <p>
      Plants vary by species, age, environment, and condition. A guide that
      works for most plants of a type may not suit your individual plant.
      If a plant is valuable, rare, or severely unwell, consider consulting a
      local nursery or plant specialist.
    </p>
    <h2>Plant Problem Solver</h2>
    <p>
      The Plant Problem Solver suggests possibilities based on the symptoms
      you describe. It is not a diagnosis. Several problems can cause
      similar symptoms, and the tool cannot see your plant. Treat its
      suggestions as a starting point for inspection, not as a definitive
      answer.
    </p>
    <h2>Safety</h2>
    <p>
      Some houseplants are toxic to people and pets if eaten. Our guides
      note toxicity where it is relevant, but this is not a complete safety
      reference. Keep plants out of reach of small children and pets where
      appropriate, and check with a veterinarian or poison control service
      if ingestion is suspected. Always wash your hands after handling soil
      and fertiliser, and follow the instructions on any product you use.
    </p>
    <h2>No guarantees</h2>
    <p>
      We do not guarantee that following a guide will save a plant, prevent
      damage, or produce any particular result. You use the information on
      this site at your own discretion.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
